maluos-session (0.5.0) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Phase 12 slice 7, the Upgrade Manager: `maluos-desk --window updates`
    (com.maluos.UpgradeManager, pinned in the dock) with four pages: Updates
    (pending, Update now, Update everything, restart, check again), Automatic
    (the switches: automatic updates on/off, security, MaluOS and Mozilla each
    on/off, restart automatically at a time), History and Release. The
    session's UpdateAction grows apply | apply-all (a terminal running pkexec
    maluctl update apply, apt's log live) and auto:… (pkexec maluctl update
    auto in a thread, the outcome in updates.last_action); the state's
    updates carry maluctl's `auto` block. The Desk's window code is shared
    (Window base class); the dock pins Firefox, Files, Settings, Software,
    the terminal, the Desk and the Upgrade Manager (favorite-apps override).
    Depends on maluos-firstboot 0.1.8 (maluctl update auto, the polkit action).
  * The Tools Installer window (`maluos-desk --window tools`,
    com.maluos.ToolsInstaller, pinned in the dock): the tools from
    maluos-tools (`maluctl tools list --json`) with their state; Install
    runs the script in a terminal, Open starts the tool, Log shows the log.
  * The Credential Manager window (`maluos-desk --window vault`,
    com.maluos.CredentialManager, pinned in the dock): the vault's full user
    side over /usr/lib/maluos/maluos_vault_client.py as the session user:
    secrets (add, show with a 30 s clipboard, rotate, delete naming the
    grants), delegations (delegate with expiry and budget, undelegate),
    requests (allow for a week or a day, deny; your own), compartments,
    backup (export and import in a terminal for the passphrase). Each
    button is one `maluctl secret` verb. Recommends maluos-vault.
  * The MaluApps window (`maluos-desk --window apps`, com.maluos.MaluApps,
    pinned in the dock): the catalogue from `maluctl office apps --json`
    (maluos-desk 0.2.0); Install, Open, Remove.

 -- Edward Honour <ed@maludb.org>  Fri, 23 Oct 2026 02:50:00 +0000

maluos-session (0.4.0) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Desk enrolment (Phase 12 slice 6): the state carries `office` (from
    /etc/maluos/office.yaml and the last heartbeat); an office thread runs
    `maluctl office heartbeat` every heartbeat_s while the person is signed
    in, with the desk token read from the vault once, and says offline on
    SIGTERM; notifications when the desk joins, when the office retires it,
    when the office is unreachable and back; OfficeAction(open|heartbeat);
    the indicator's Office submenu; the Desk's Office group on System.

 -- Edward Honour <ed@maludb.org>  Thu, 22 Oct 2026 16:30:00 +0000

maluos-session (0.3.1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * The updates reading runs in its own thread: opening the apt cache can
    take minutes under emulation and must not stall the poll loop, the bus
    or the notifications. Refresh() no longer forces an apt re-read;
    UpdateAction refresh does. Failed readings retry after two minutes.

 -- Edward Honour <ed@maludb.org>  Thu, 22 Oct 2026 12:43:31 +0000

maluos-session (0.3.0) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Software updates (Phase 12 slice 5): the state carries maluctl update
    status (pending by source, automatic policy, restart due), re-read when
    apt or dpkg state changes and every 15 minutes; one notification for
    updates that wait for the user (Install opens GNOME Software's updates
    page) and one for a due restart; UpdateAction(open|restart|refresh) on
    the bus; an Updates line in the indicator; a System page in the Desk.
  * gsettings override: GNOME Software does not notify about downloaded
    updates itself (the session does).

 -- Edward Honour <ed@maludb.org>  Thu, 22 Oct 2026 02:18:18 +0000

maluos-session (0.2.0) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Phase 12 slice 3. Agents carry their owner (MALUOS_AGENT_OWNER) and are
    marked yours in the state and the menu; the vault's pending grant
    requests for your secrets are in the state, in the menu with Allow and
    Deny, and become notifications with Allow and Deny buttons
    (org.freedesktop.Notifications actions); RequestDecide on D-Bus.
  * MaluOS Desk (maluos-desk): a libadwaita window on the same state with
    pages for agents, models, vault and alerts, and a desktop entry.

 -- Edward Honour <ed@maludb.org>  Tue, 20 Oct 2026 20:40:00 +0000

maluos-session (0.1.1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Notifications are sent asynchronously with a 30 s limit: a shell that
    is slow to answer (software rendering in a VM, a busy session) no
    longer stalls the poll loop, and a late answer is no longer a failure.
    Seen in the emulated UEFI boot test.

 -- Edward Honour <ed@maludb.org>  Tue, 20 Oct 2026 17:40:00 +0000

maluos-session (0.1.0) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Phase 12 slice 2: the agent-aware session. maluos-desktop-session, a
    per-user D-Bus service (com.maluos.Session) that watches agent units
    through systemd, the gateway and the vault through their sockets as
    the session user, and the user's ledger alerts; state changes become
    desktop notifications. The GNOME Shell extension
    maluos-session@maluos.com shows the state in the top panel and offers
    start/stop/restart of agents through polkit. Enabled in the MaluOS
    session by a gsettings override.

 -- Edward Honour <ed@maludb.org>  Mon, 19 Oct 2026 20:00:00 +0000
